    "body": "Triage, checked on `main` 8f30bee.\n\n**What a posted program says today:** the only comment is the machine name after the program number (`block([\"O0001\", \"(\" + nm + \")\"])` in `fanuc.cps`; the other dialects are similar). There's nothing per operation or per tool, apart from the wear-compensation note (#38).\n\n**What a post already has to write comments from:** every section's stream (`crates/post/src/post/mod.rs::dump`) carries `OperationName`, `ToolDiameter`, `WorkOffset`, `Coolant` and the stock box as `PARAM` records. `onToolChange(number, name)` gets the tool's number and library name. So these need **no stream change**, only script lines:\n- per section: `(OPERATION: Contour1 - G54)`;\n- per tool change: `(T01 EM-0600-4FL D6.)`.\n\n**What needs new stream records:** the tool's kind and corner radius or tip angle (\"6 mm flat end mill, 4 flutes\"), the operation's kind (\"2D Contour\") and the setup's name. Those would be new `PARAM`s in `dump`. That's small, but it touches the CL stream format, so it's worth deciding once.\n\n**Cost:** every posted program changes, so all 102 conformance goldens under `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/` (seven dialects) plus the top-level Fanuc goldens get regenerated, and reviewed once. Comment syntax differs per dialect: `( )` for Fanuc, Haas, Mazak and Tormach, `;` for Sinumerik and Heidenhain. A comment must also never carry a `(` or `)` from a user's operation or tool name, so names need sanitising per dialect. Some controls refuse nested parentheses.\n\n**Suggested shape:** comments behind a post property (on by default, or off to keep goldens stable). That fits the per-post property list proposed in #258's triage (part 3), so a shop that wants bare programs keeps them.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
